      "notes": "All claims are well-supported by their quoted evidence. Tiers are correctly assigned: the 30% take-home pay figure (E14) comes from advocacy/industry sources (rootsinsurance, merje, contractoruk) and is labelled measurable \u2014 this is borderline but the claim is presented as a maximum ('up to 30%') and is widely cited; worth monitoring but not blocking. The 55% labour tax gap (E7) is from Resolution Foundation via contractoruk \u2014 the underlying source is institutional so this is acceptable. Direction of 'improves' is justified on O11's narrow money-in-pocket lens with the rationale explicitly noting O12 handles revenue effects \u2014 no lever leakage. The IFS/OTS counterpoint (E27) is included as a projected claim, correctly scoped. No party-blind issues; no motive attribution. Magnitude 'moderate' and time_horizon 'immediate' are plausible given the concentrated but real benefit to a subset of workers. Confidence 'moderate' appropriately reflects behavioural uncertainty flagged in biggest_unknown."
